INT. CATERING VAN, PARKED BEHIND SYMPHONY HALL - NIGHT

Metal shelving. Trays of canapés. A thermos. Four people in black waiter uniforms crowd the back of the van, their tuxedo jackets half-unbuttoned.

JOSEFINA "FINA" QUISPE-LARSEN (40s, crew boss) unrolls a blueprint on a cooler lid. TREVOR ASANTE (30s, gloves, a canvas bag) checks a watch. OLIVIA BRANDT (20s, earpiece, nervous) tucks a cable under her cuff. And WALLACE "WALLY" DRUMMOND (60s, an actual caterer's apron over the tux) props a tray against the door.

FINA
Vault's under the cello section. Trevor goes in through the green room. Olivia takes the stairs. Wally, you walk the floor with the canapés.

WALLY
I'm not a thief, I'm a caterer.

FINA
Today you're both.

TREVOR
The guard rotates at ten twenty.

OLIVIA
Ten twenty-two. I checked.

TREVOR
It's ten twenty.

OLIVIA
I checked the rotation, not the time.

WALLY
Children. Children.

FINA
We have six minutes. Trevor, the bag.

Trevor hands her the canvas bag. She unzips it. Out come four tuxedo vests, each with a small lump sewn in. She tosses them around. They catch them, fumble, button up.

OLIVIA
Is this a camera?

TREVOR
It's a microphone. The camera is in Wally's tray.

WALLY
There's a camera in my tray?

TREVOR
There's a camera in the pâté.

WALLY
I'll never serve pâté again.

FINA
Wally, go. Smile. Walk slowly. The vault door opens at ten twenty-six.

Wally lifts the tray. Pushes the van door open. Trevor slips out behind him; Olivia follows; Fina climbs down last, closing the door softly as she goes.

Outside, footsteps crunch gravel. A flashlight beam swings across the van's windshield.

The four freeze. Wally lowers the tray. Trevor holds his breath. Olivia grips her cuff. Fina's hand slides to the door latch.

WALLY
(whispering)
Do I smile?

FINA
Smile.

He smiles. The beam slides across his face, hesitates, moves on. Gravel crunches away. Wally exhales so hard his tray shakes.
